  "details": "There are quite a few seat/station-related Canny posts, but here's another I'd like to throw:\n\nSome legacy avatars and worlds will have VRChat stations that might have a large proximity range. I can be 30 meters away from a chair and accidentally \"snipe\" it (by clicking on it, and getting teleported into the far-away chair), consequently, having to run back or fix IK bugs caused by the station.\n\nI would like to override seat proximity where I would like be comfortable with clicking on a station 1 meter away from me, or 50cm away from me. Maybe I'm stingy, and want my hand to be right on the dot to be able to click and sit in the station.\n\nFor implementation, the proximity would likely have to be dependent on the hand bone, versus the head or chest bone for proximity settings like earmuffs. In addition, there should also still be a proximity marker or visualizer shown for reference, especially if I would like to scale it down to centimeter length.",
